{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And if he strikes.</b> HaShem commanded that the slave go free in place of his eye or his tooth, so that his master not be cruel and strike him a severe blow; for if he destroys his eye or even his tooth, he goes free from his authority and he loses his property."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:05.345751927Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}